00:04:12.533 --> 00:04:14.431
Intuition: packing for a trip.

67
00:04:14.711 --> 00:04:16.674
You don't weigh every shirt before a trip.

68
00:04:16.954 --> 00:04:17.743
You think:

69
00:04:18.023 --> 00:04:21.799
5 days, 1 shirt per day, plus 2 spare, so 7 shirts.

70
00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:23.573
That fits in a cabin bag.

71
00:04:23.853 --> 00:04:28.909
That's back-of-the-envelope estimation: rough numbers, simple arithmetic, a decision.

72
00:04:29.189 --> 00:04:33.477
The goal is being right within a factor of 2 to 3, not within 1 %.

73
00:04:33.757 --> 00:04:36.103
A factor-of-10 error changes the design.

74
00:04:36.383 --> 00:04:40.074
A factor-of-2 error usually changes only the instance count.

